th"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied. usb-storage was blocked immediately and remained blocked through an observed reboot. The mandatory node-restart protocol is coherent and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":["No workload-specific data or multi-node cluster existed in the captured topology, so restart recovery evidence is limited to OS health, writable storage, retained configuration, and the required module behavior.","Testing used an explicit modprobe attempt rather than a physical USB-storage hot-plug event; the effective install-deny rule and post-reboot load failure nevertheless directly test kernel-module loading."]}
